# Milestone: M3 (updated v0.10.9-tag-state W2; v0.10.15-vm-decomp-2: bound scope)
# Covers: TAG_STOP is not intercepted by a try/catch block; the catch clause
#         is skipped and TAG_STOP continues propagating outward.
#
# Activated: v0.10.7 W7 — Tag.new() + tag.stop() shipped (v0.10.2 W4).
# Old label: T29
#
# Semantics: the unwind walker absorbs UEXEC_THROW in UCLEANUP_TRY_FRAME but
# does NOT absorb UEXEC_TAG_STOP; TAG_STOP propagates past catch clauses.
# `Realm.caught` remains 0 confirming catch was not executed.
#
# v0.10.15-vm-decomp-2 (v0.10.9-B): OP_PUSH_TAG now binds the `t:` scope to the
# user tag t, so `t.stop()` from inside is a clean tag-stop on t's own active
# scope — NOT the D3 outside-scope fatal that v0.10.9 emitted (when `t:` made an
# anonymous UTag unbound to t).  The tag-stop scope block evaluates to `nil`;
# catch is still skipped (TAG_STOP is not absorbed by UCLEANUP_TRY_FRAME), so
# `Realm.caught` stays 0.  This fixture now pins the bound-scope catch-skip
# semantic.  Workspace-root compatibility-decisions ledger §S5c.

var t = Tag.new()
var caught = 0
t: { try { t.stop() } catch (e) { Realm.caught = 1 } }
Realm.caught
[00000000] <Tag>
[00000000] 0
[00000000] nil
[00000001] 0
